101 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 67 0 R
/T (The website that actually worked for me was keybr.com. This was where I finally improved so much. It really lets you get a feel for touch typing, and personally I found its statistics interesting, and it was one of the things that motivated me to continue since I felt like I was improving. Occasionally I'd watch videos on youtube about how to improve touch typing and people who are actually fast. One of the first videos was pretty much just someone trying out keybr and he showed his results after one month of practicing. I was impressed by that and wanted to give keybr a try. I really like the design and experience of the website and instantly got hooked on it. This was also when I was really into the idea of muscle memory.)
/E (The website that actually worked for me was keybr.com. This was where I finally improved so much. It really lets you get a feel for touch typing, and personally I found its statistics interesting, and it was one of the things that motivated me to continue since I felt like I was improving. Occasionally I'd watch videos on youtube about how to improve touch typing and people who are actually fast. One of the first videos was pretty much just someone trying out keybr and he showed his results after one month of practicing. I was impressed by that and wanted to give keybr a try. I really like the design and experience of the website and instantly got hooked on it. This was also when I was really into the idea of muscle memory.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2 3]
>>
