/T (Ok I guess I did say that there's no specific WPM that's considered fast at the start. However, you can be fast relative to others. Most people average ~40 WPM. Honestly, your WPM would actually really depend on the conditions. A 60-second test would be more accurate than a 15-second test and also test your endurance. 15-second or even 10 word tests just show your burst speed. Punctuation and numbers also would matter, but personally I just use letters when practicing and comparing my speed. Also FYI WPM is assumed to be 5 characters per word.)
/E (Ok I guess I did say that there's no specific WPM that's considered fast at the start. However, you can be fast relative to others. Most people average ~40 WPM. Honestly, your WPM would actually really depend on the conditions. A 60-second test would be more accurate than a 15-second test and also test your endurance. 15-second or even 10 word tests just show your burst speed. Punctuation and numbers also would matter, but personally I just use letters when practicing and comparing my speed. Also FYI WPM is assumed to be 5 characters per word.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
