/T (Remember: always prioritize accuracy first before speed. Touch typing is probably the most optimized technique for typing, so I'd recommend that. You don't have to use ALL 10 fingers; most people who touch type probably only use 9 fingers \(only using the dominant thumb for the spacebar\), including me.)
/E (Remember: always prioritize accuracy first before speed. Touch typing is probably the most optimized technique for typing, so I'd recommend that. You don't have to use ALL 10 fingers; most people who touch type probably only use 9 fingers \(only using the dominant thumb for the spacebar\), including me.)
