/T (It'll feel pretty slow and painful at first, but it will be worth it, and you'll really see improvements once you develop total muscle memory for each key. I think you shouldn't really use multiplayer typing websites \(like typeracer\) to actually improve. I'd normally just do it for fun and would rather practice mostly by myself. I also think practicing on just letters is enough, really. You can practice numbers and punctuation if you want; they'd still be pretty useful in actual situations.)
/E (It'll feel pretty slow and painful at first, but it will be worth it, and you'll really see improvements once you develop total muscle memory for each key. I think you shouldn't really use multiplayer typing websites \(like typeracer\) to actually improve. I'd normally just do it for fun and would rather practice mostly by myself. I also think practicing on just letters is enough, really. You can practice numbers and punctuation if you want; they'd still be pretty useful in actual situations.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [1]
